It may not feel like it came from nowhere—you may be drawing on repeated experiences—but repeated experiences can still be unrepresentative, especially if they’re concentrated in busy commercial or high-density areas.

I can’t endorse “Bangladeshis are loud and quarrelsome” as a general fact. It’s more accurate to separate:

- what you observed in particular places;
- what conditions may have contributed (crowding, traffic, nightlife, stress, unfamiliarity);
- what you prefer personally (lower noise, less confrontation).

That framing takes your discomfort seriously without turning it into a judgment about an entire nationality.
